WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.340
- But one thing I love
that you talk about,

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:05.060
and I think it was actually
a couple of years ago

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:06.460
maybe even that you first
started talking about it,

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:07.330
people were like, "Oh my gosh,

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:08.550
2020 is going to be the detriment of it."

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.620
Or like, "It's gonna,
everything is horrible.

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:12.770
It's the apocalypse" and I loved,

00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:15.210
that you said, it takes some
times that deconstructing,

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:17.080
that blowing up a things,

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:21.930
to actually sort out all the
crap that's actually wrong.

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:24.150
Are you hopeful or are
you still kind of like,

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.720
Oh my gosh, like what's happening?

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:28.620
- Two things, I mean, I

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:31.740
used the word apocalypse,
apocalypse means uncovering.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.300
- Yeah, right?
- So in terms of

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.290
what this time is doing,

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:37.050
none of this, none of this is happening.

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.770
None of this injustice and
inequality is new at all, right?

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:42.617
Which is why, my activist
friends aren't the ones saying,

00:00:42.617 --> 00:00:45.030
"Oh my God, 2020 is the worst."

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.330
They're actually feeling hopeful,

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:48.110
because this is, all of this inequality

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:49.590
has been going on for a very long time.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:52.010
It's just that now people
are finally seeing it

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:55.720
because of the apocalypse
uncovering of COVID.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.110
As to whether I'm hopeful or not,

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:59.260
I heard Stacey Abrams say the other day,

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:00.490
someone said, "Are you hopeful?"

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:03.160
And she said, "I am neither
hopeful nor pessimistic.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:04.670
I am determined."

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:07.030
- Oh,
- I love that so much.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:09.460
Because, as someone who's sober,

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:11.710
I rely on what I can control.

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:14.090
And I know what I can't
control is outcome.

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:17.180
So pessimism and optimism
are relying on outcome.

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:20.070
But determinism, being determined,

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:22.040
that all has to do with our input.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:24.030
How we're showing up, right?

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:28.100
So what I know is I am
determined over the next weeks

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:31.080
to get to every single
untamed woman I know

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:33.140
to refuse being gaslit,

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.280
to know what she knows,
feel what she feels,

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.670
and to show up at the polls, November 3rd.

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:40.270
- Amen, Alicia,
(applause)

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:42.430
How are you feeling about everything

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:44.000
like voting and everything?

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:44.833
I know that,

00:01:44.833 --> 00:01:46.520
everybody always gets
frustrated with people

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:48.260
in the music and the music
world, and the art world.

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:49.910
And they're like just,
you know, be artistic.

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:50.743
And I'm like,

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:52.600
"Yes, but also like I'm not
pushing my views on you.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:54.250
But you have to realize how,

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:55.550
I think, because we've traveled,

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:57.930
we see how lucky we are,
how fortunate we are,

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:59.200
to be able to vote."

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.920
I don't know, I feel like
it's kind of your duty

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:04.240
as an American citizen to say
something like that, you know?

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:05.100
- I mean, it is.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.950
It is all of our responsibility.

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:09.562
It's all of our opportunity.

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:11.580
And definitely it is.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:14.170
It is, it's something that we all should

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:17.297
feel really actually excited

00:02:17.297 --> 00:02:20.650
and passionate about, you know?

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:22.590
We can all learn so much more.

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:24.720
I think that's one thing
that I think about a lot.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:26.020
You don't have to know it all.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:28.080
I think that's one of the
things that feels intimidating.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:31.510
You're like, "Whoa, I'm not
sure and how about this, and"

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:32.960
It's okay that you don't know it all.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:35.500
And it's okay to actually
start to learn more.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.900
I think that's something
that I'm asking my friends

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:39.590
and family and also just

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:42.370
you know, anybody who's
connecting with me.

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:44.420
I'm like, let's take a moment to actually

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:46.050
dig into the parts that we don't know.

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:47.580
Let's dig into the parts of the ballot

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.780
that maybe we are a little
bit insecure about or,

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:52.430
the names that we're not so clear about,

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:55.430
or the policies that maybe
don't make perfect sense or,

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:57.980
that we didn't take the time
to look into enough yet.

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:00.230
It's okay, it's all a growing process,

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:04.130
and it's all a part of
actively being a human being.

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:07.080
You know, and actively being
able to be a participant

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:10.120
in what this whole thing looks
like, you know what I mean?

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:11.200
This is up to us.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:12.667
This is not thing where it's like,

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:16.110
"Oh, we're gonna hope that that one guy

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:18.240
or woman does the thing."

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:22.900
No, one person can't do
anything all by themselves.

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:24.650
We all need to show up.

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:26.020
We have to show up for our families,

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:27.600
for our own kids

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:28.760
for our sisters and brothers,

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:30.020
for our communities.

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:31.100
Because if we're not showing up,

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:31.937
no one else is gonna be like

00:03:31.937 --> 00:03:33.750
"Oh, hey, what's happening in your spot?

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:35.310
'Cause I care so much about you."

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:38.460
No, we have to care about our selves.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:42.150
We have to care about
ourselves enough to show up.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:43.600
So it's less about

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:45.540
that they're gonna do all this stuff,

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:47.650
and what, and we gotta show up for us.

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:49.600
You know, less about them, more about us.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:51.640
And let's learn about what we can

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:53.680
so that we can align with people that have

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:55.220
similar beliefs and thoughts.

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:56.840
But man, this is for us.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:58.330
We gotta do this.

